               Traversal + Maximum
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 40, 20, 70, 30};

        int max = arr[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] > max) {
                max = arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println(max);
    }
}

              Traversal + Minimum.
int[] arr = {40, 10, 30, 5, 20};

int min = arr[0];

for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] < min) {
        min = arr[i];
    }
}

System.out.println(min);
                        search
there are two types:
linear search and binary serach



                       linear search
it checks one by one element to until it archieve the target.
Why is it called Linear Search?

Because we're moving in a straight sequence:
                           program
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] n = {1, 2, 34, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10};
        int target = 10;

        for (int i = 0; i < n.length; i++) {

            if (n[i] == target) {
                System.out.println(i);
                break;
            }
        }
    }
}
                 
